{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["And behold, the prophet rebukes them that they should show kindness to the wayfarers by giving them water to drink, just as he rebuked Moab (Deuteronomy 23:5)." "<b>To meet the thirsty, etc.</b> The heh of the feminine in place of alef:" "<b>Tema.</b> Like Hadad and Tema (Genesis 25:15):" "<b>With bread.</b> It returns to the thirsty, and the meaning is: show kindness to him, for it was his custom to feed every wanderer who came to him:" "And the meaning of <b>his troops</b> is his men or his companions:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:33.610352663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}